---
source: crates/cli/tests/native.rs
expression: run.stdout
---
Fast, native developer tools

Usage: tw <COMMAND>

Commands:
  json         Format, minify and validate JSON, written as jq . writes it
  convert      Between JSON, YAML 1.2, TOML, CSV and XML
  base64       Encode and decode Base64 (RFC 4648)
  url          Percent-encode and decode text for URLs
  jwt          Decode, verify and create JSON Web Tokens (RFC 7519)
  md5sum       MD5 checksums of files, or check them
  sha1sum      SHA-1 checksums of files, or check them
  sha256sum    SHA-256 checksums of files, or check them
  sha512sum    SHA-512 checksums of files, or check them
  b2sum        BLAKE2b checksums of files, or check them
  uuid         Generate UUIDs: random (v4) or time-ordered (v7)
  time         Unix timestamps, ISO 8601 and RFC dates, in any time zone
  cron         What a cron expression means, and when it runs next
  regex        Test a pattern, see its matches and groups, replace with it
  diff         Compare two files line by line, as GNU diff does
  case         One name in every case code uses: camelCase, snake_case, kebab-case…
  base         A number in binary, octal, decimal, hex or any base from 2 to 36
  jq           Query and transform JSON, as jq 1.8 does
  list         List every tool
  completions  Print shell completions
  help         Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -h, --help     Print help
  -V, --version  Print version
